A config dir claude was never onboarded in: it holds neither of the two files
ReadDirCapabilities probes — settings.json and .claude.json — so the dir cannot be
spoken for at all, and every axis is unknown rather than empty. An earlier version
also read settings.local.json; that read was removed, because claude resolves its
local settings source against the project root and never looks for it here.

This is the shape a pool member takes when its config_dir was typed correctly but
never logged into, so the remedy is to set it up (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=<dir> claude, then
/login) rather than to check the path. The file is here only because git does not
track empty directories.
